                <pb facs="0701" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/186: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-19T12:00:00-06:00">June 19,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>128. The President of Honduras informs me that yesterday Government forces under
                    General Torribio Ramos defeated Ferrera decisively at Jaral which is located at
                    north end of Lake Yojoa. He states that at least 70 of the insurgents were slain
                    and that Ferrera is now fleeing westward with 90 men.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
